   result:
   REF_DEV arm.bignum_add_p384.BIGNUM_ADD_P384_CORRECT ok=true seconds=269.631 axioms=3

Reading: in A the Z term reaching the selection is the simulator's nested
per-step condition.  Its bitval subterms --
   &2 pow 64 <= &(val sum_s12) + &(bitval (...))
   &(val sum_s4) < &18446744069414584320 + &(bitval (...))
   &(val sum_s3) < &4294967295
 -- are unconstrained atoms in the word instance: no accumulator relation for
steps 15--22 exists to say they are the carries/borrows of those word
operations, so SAT sets them to falsify output = ref_add.  In B the same term
is the two-bit word test on carry_s12 and carry_s22, and carry_s22 is pinned
by the accumulator relation of the last flag-only step (ADCS X3 X3 XZR), which
consumes carry_s21, carry_s20, ... down to the SBCS chain; the residual is
UNSAT and the branch closes.  This isolates the cause to the derive_steps
admission (commit 60ddf31), not to the bridge and not to the arithmetic lemmas.
